			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847853">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Second Revision</strong></p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Comedy, Emotional (might be just an emotional piece)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> When first entering the article, you will only be able to see the part of the SCP that's dangerous i.e. the computervirus that keeps on printing out the credentials of a bankrupt business. Scrolling down you will find a &quot;insert clearance 4/XXXX&quot; which will reveal the factory part of the SCP which is classified as safe, potentially thaumiel</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> This SCP is a 2 part Anomaly: Part 1 is a computerprogram that is able to crack open many cybersecurity features (not all) and then infects every possible device that is able to physically print out a message (printer, fax machines, 3d printer). 2nd Part is a warehouse, which location is included inside the printed messages. This warehouse houses a giant machine which is able to produce anomalies that could end up as thaumiel if improved.<br />
Efforts are ongoing to find the individual, who created this SCP.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> &quot;Our business relationship has to come to an abruptive end before they even really began. I have no more funds to spare and only failures to sell. It has been a pleasure trying to do business.&quot; is the message getting printed out by many different devices all over germany. Attached to it are the credentials of a bankrupt business. The foundation covers this incident up and pushes updates that make the virus unable to infect more devices. The source does not get found and efforts are ongoing. The business mentioned is located on an untouched coal reserve that has been bought by a coal mining company. This factory is supposed to create thaumiel SCPs and then sell them to the foundation. This factory is supposed to tell the story of how one individual tried building up a business with this idea and how this coal company ruined them by denying them access to much needed ressources. This story and the purpose of this factory are written down in a digital form by the missing individual. All testing is halted until the mysterious individual is found. The Individual will be found and tries to improve this SCP but is unable to stop the computervirus he released. Testing logs of prototypes by said individual included.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> A story of medium length of how an SCP got made without malicious intent, made to aid the foundation. Also includes testing logs by someone not from the foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
The individual, who made this SCP, is not anomalous in nature. They found out about the foundation after witnessing them contain an SCP without getting noticed himself (thorough as the foundation might be) and then began to educate himself on how to make anomalies (not yet specified, more research needed).</p>
</div>
