<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<h1><span>Questions I Have While Reading Through</span></h1>
<blockquote>
<p>A warehouse which has anomalous properties that could give it the thaumiel classification and which produces all kinds of objects that share that sentiment.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, so what about it is those properties?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The warehouse gets discovered and testing ensues. At first the researchers are enthusiastic and hopeful of being able to find anomalies with which they might be able to contain really hazardous or hard to contain SCPs but get gradually more and more frustrated as their research shows what a waste of time this warehouse and its contents are.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>But if its thaumiel, how is this a waste of their time?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This would however reclassify this anomaly as Euclid since it is sentient so i would leave that part out.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This isn't entirely true. But it could be an interesting addition to the story. It may fall prey to the whole &quot;Ending on a note&quot; thing.</p>
<hr />
<h1><span>final notes</span></h1>
<p>I actually think this is interesting, I quite like it and I'm willing to leave a <span style="color: green">GREENLIGHT</span> on this, it seems like if you play this right, it could end up being super heartfelt and sweet. I suggest dropping the comedy thing altogether. Though, It almost reminds me of Wanders hat from Wander Over Yonder.</p>
<p>Good luck!</p>
