<p>Thank you very much!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Okay, so what about it is those properties?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was thinking about it being able to completely shield the exterior from harm caused by things inside the warehouse i.e. nuking the warehouse from the inside would not transmit the shockwave or heat to the outside. So you could for example put 079 in there and let someone look at a photograph of his but 079 would not be able to leave since he would cause harm to the world outside of the warehouse.</p>
<p>The problem with this warehouse being that anything from the outside can still cause harm to the warehouse and the inside of it especially. I was thinking along the lines that they wanted to make a small containment area inside of it, then began testing the durability of the walls and discovered that if you put a hole in the wall of this SCP from the outside, all organic matter inside the warehouse gets violently sucked through the hole making the warehouse not really useable for containment.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>But if its thaumiel, how is this a waste of their time?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My idea was that it gets hastily classified as Thaumiel because the useful properties get discovered way before any of the over-the-top drawbacks get discovered making it not thaumiel but safe instead</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This isn't entirely true. But it could be an interesting addition to the story. It may fall prey to the whole &quot;Ending on a note&quot; thing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>oh, good to know. i though all sentient SCPs are immediately Euclid since sentients is somewhat unpredictable. Also, i dont really know myself how i would make the note work soooo&#8230; Might leave it out, Might not. Will have to see how it looks when i m done writing it</p>
<p>thanks again!</p>

