																		Re: Thaumiel Factory Failure (seeking greenlight)
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608689338" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608686468 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">23 Dec 2020 01:21</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4851439">
									

<p>Responded:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>They don't. They simply try to manufacture Objects that could aid the foundation, who would then in turn be classified as Thaumiel.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not all objects that could be helpful are given the Thaumiel class. If this person is only churning out items that would be considered Thaumiel, that's a difficult to believe level of specificity and ability.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This is the reason this individual does not speak to the foundation at all while building the factory. They want the products to speak for themselves.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again, why would they assume the Foundation would use the products to begin with, especially if they don't have any insight into the production and motive behind the items?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>he thinks that the foundation in its entirety is completely good and would never do anything evil.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Given that the Foundation would have had to be ridiculously sloppy in order for the person to witness a single event that makes them understand that there's a whole shadow organization that is intent on containing the anomalous, this is difficult to believe. You as the author inherently know everything ahead of time, but your character needs to learn in a believable manner if you want the audience to take the story seriously.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This Person does not happen to have it. He builds it himself. How he does that is something I am still working on. Plan is currently that he uses his money to hire people that know a thing or two and compiles their knowledge.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The issue with this is that it's overpowered and contrived. You have so many unlikely elements already, the fact that the guy inherits money, the fact that he wasn't noticed by the Foundation during a containment event, the fact that he hires people to make anomalies somehow, and so on. Each of these traits separately is already potentially skepticism-raising; combining so many of these coincidences just makes for a story that feels sloppily made up and fake.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>things he thinks are useful like gloves that make your hands indestructable, boxes that lock things inside with no way of opening them from the inside, glasses that protect your mind from seeing things and hazmat suits to keep nasty stuff away.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since none of these things can be reliably used to observably contain anomalies, they wouldn't be classified as Thaumiel.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I want the factory to have 1 important person in charge, who hired other people to help him build it, yet him pulling all the strings.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This doesn't answer my question of <em>why</em> you want only one person.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I am open to any changes that make the story better/clearer without completely changing its direction.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like for this to stand more of a chance with the audience, you need to change the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>don't have just one person in charge. Have at least two or three friends/family members. If you just have one person, they'll seem like a too-important overpowered Mary Sue character.</li>
<li>don't have them witness a Foundation containment and somehow go unnoticed. Have someone they are close to be involved in an incident, and maybe taken into Foundation custody. When the person goes looking, they find a Foundation agent checking up on the amnesticized someone and the agent gives some very brief information about being with an organization that &quot;helps after disasters&quot; or something. Your character talks to their friend/whoever who was in the incident, and wants to start helping the people who saved their friend/whoever. This will make more sense than your current setup.</li>
<li>don't have the setup be for a factory, which implies mass production and cut corners for many exact copies of the same product. Use &quot;workshop&quot; or the like. This will make the Foundation more interested in testing the items as individual anomalies rather than just locking all of the stuff up as repeat junk.</li>
</ul>
<p>There will definitely be more changes needed after these, but that's what I would start with.</p>
</div>
</div>
